That error happens because retire is a file, not a folder (directory). The cd command can only open folders.
To look inside the directory where retire lives, you must stop at the bin/ folder.
## 1. Go to the Folder
Run this command to navigate to the correct directory:

cd /home/user/.nvm/versions/node/v22.23.2/bin/

## 2. Verify the File Exists
Once you are inside that folder, list the files to see retire by running:

ls -l retire

------------------------------
## Reminders on Using retire

* Do not use cd to run it: You do not need to be in this folder to use the tool. Because it is globally installed, typing retire anywhere in your system will execute it.
* To check if it works: Just type retire --version from your home directory to see if it responds correctly.

If you are trying to view or edit the actual source code of retire, let me know. I can show you how to use the cat or nano commands to open the file directly without changing directories.
